<p>Ukraine launched a large overnight drone attack on Russia, killing at least four people — three in the Moscow region and one in Belgorod — Russian local authorities said Sunday. Russia’s Defence Ministry said air defences downed 556 drones overnight and into the morning, and officials said Moscow faced its biggest drone attack in more than a year. Moscow region Governor Andrey Vorobyov said two men died in Pogorelki after debris from a downed drone fell on a home-construction site, and a woman died in Khimki when a drone struck an apartment block. Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin said 12 people were wounded in the capital, most near the entrance to Moscow’s oil refinery, and that the refinery’s “technology” was not damaged. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy confirmed the strikes and said Ukraine was justified in responding to Russian attacks on Ukrainian cities. The Indian embassy in Russia said one Indian worker was killed and three others were injured in the Moscow region attack, and that embassy officials visited the site and the injured workers at a hospital.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/dkD3c4Vg1SECIDu1nRfo4LOqtoL3NlQZ1NRoozP2pA8L2YA0ljgStdLU0eJxF7mFQlucVuLuGm70H1iUdtjuO7a0euDcBRQOLzgCqM2YspfEOAY2jDlHZhgJ2XT07hi9u--L2J64cWwFbxTE7Dad9KwSh2SqQDA3vMwtvToSdzpDRZZxr0rykL5JDp6uU-pa5-FqsVQq0O0G-w' alt='A damaged residential building in Krasnogorsk, in the Moscow region of Russia, on Sunday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Belgorod detail: Local authorities said one man was killed when a drone struck a truck in the Belgorod region, which borders Ukraine.</li><li>Wider strikes: The Russian Defence Ministry said drones were reported across 14 Russian regions, Crimea and the Black and Azov seas.</li><li>Ukraine hit: Ukrainian authorities said Russian drone strikes overnight wounded eight people in Ukraine.</li><li>Recent Kyiv toll: The attack followed Russian strikes on Kyiv that killed at least 24 people, accounts citing Ukrainian authorities said.</l